    "content": "Saint Mary's College of California, located in Moraga, is a private Catholic, Lasallian institution with a 420-acre campus near San Francisco, enrolling around 4,000 students. It offers undergraduate and graduate programs, including business and liberal arts. The 2024 acceptance rate was 86.53%, with tuition at approximately $56,134 for 2023-2024. Key Details for Saint Mary's College of California (Moraga, CA): Admissions & Academics: Known for a close-knit community, the college focuses on \"Shared Inquiry\" and liberal arts, with notable programs in Business Administration and Economics. Admissions Difficulty: With an 86.53% acceptance rate, it is generally accessible. Tuition: For the 2023–2024 academic year, tuition was $56,134. Notable Alumni: The college has over 60 notable alumni, including NBA players Patty Mills and Matthew Dellavedova, as well as baseball Hall of Famer Harry Hooper. Location: Situated 21 miles east of San Francisco, offering a suburban, residential setting. Important Distinction: This information refers to Saint Mary's College of California in Moraga, CA. It is often confused with Saint Mary's College in Notre Dame, Indiana, a historic women's college (founded 1844) near South Bend, which is a separate institution.",
